# Set tokens in your HTTP client's private environment; do not commit credentials.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Current profile and ETag
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Provision an institutional user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: provision-researcher-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identitySubject": "institutional-researcher-subject",
  "institutionalId": "A01234567",
  "email": "researcher@university.example",
  "displayName": "Researcher",
  "roles": ["RESEARCHER"]
}

### Update your profile using the ETag from GET /me
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{"displayName":"Updated Name","locale":"es-MX"}

### Evaluate resource access as an authorized workload
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/v1/authorization/check
Authorization: Bearer {{serviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectId": "{{userId}}",
  "action": "PROJECT_READ",
  "resource": {"type":"PROJECT","id":"{{projectId}}"}
}
